        "original_id": "6ad6cf1b-8612-5967-b163-885a5761c2d0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Pioneer Helmet, Benty Grange helmet\n- People: Thomas Bateman\n- Places: Benty Grange Farm, Monyash, Derbyshire\n- Concepts: Anglo-Saxon archaeology, boar crest symbolism, Beowulf\n\nFacts:\n- On 3 May 1848, Thomas Bateman excavated the Benty Grange helmet from an Anglo-Saxon tumulus at Benty Grange Farm in Monyash, Derbyshire.\n- The Benty Grange helmet is an archaeological artefact.\n- The Pioneer Helmet has a simple iron boar crest on top.\n- The Pioneer Helmet’s boar crest associates it with the Benty Grange helmet, the Guilden Morden boar, and descriptions in the poem Beowulf from the same period.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
